        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="BUR17" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Charles</forename>
                        <surname>Burton</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1760">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1847"/>
                    <occupation>Lawyer/Judge</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See Ed Pope: There were a number of prominent people named Burton in
                            Ireland in 1800 (Sir Charles Burton baronet of Polarton, co. Carlow son
                            of Sir Charles Hist Irish Parl 1702-1775 / Francis Burton Dict Irish
                            Biog d.1828 surgeon / William Henry Burton Dict Irish Biog 1739-1818 /
                            Francis Nathaniel Nurton Hist Irish Parl 1766-1832) but this is likely
                            to have been Charles Burton 1760-1847 (Judges in Ireland, E Elrington
                            Ball, vol2 p341) who became Curran's chief assistant (see L Hale, John
                            Philpot Curran pp87-8, 273). We have not included under this entry the Burton of
                            1814 associated with Godwin's financial affairs, but the entries of
                            October 1817 around Curran's death were very likely Charles Burton
                            again, the last two entries in 1819 and 1832 are not so likely to
                            have been him. </p>
                    </note>
